cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this protocol or the accompanying code, please use the metadata below."
title: "Three gates, three proxies: auditing the null-report checks of a pre-registered LLM-agent evaluation"
# This abstract must match the Abstract section of manuscript/main.md verbatim.
# analysis/scripts/check_claim_boundary.py compares them on every run, so editing
# one without the other fails repro.sh.
abstract: >-
  We audit the three gates by which one of our pre-registered evaluations fixed in advance what a
  null result would be worth. The evaluation asked whether a channel from a language-model agent's
  recent movement to its sampling settings, in practice two fixed sampling settings, shifts which of
  five zones it names next by more than a total-variation margin of 0.10. Each gate ran as written
  but read a proxy for the quantity its reading depends on. The entropy floor decided the reported
  branch, stopping the rules on the second of two models although each context and condition
  produced two to four zones. Simulated post hoc on an assumed truth from that model's draws, at its
  declared shifts only, the deciding test detects a margin-sized shift in all 500 replicates of each
  of four feasible directions, with the floor stopping 353, 452, 500 and 49 of them. The power gate,
  which left the branch unchanged, reads the power of a chi-square surrogate, not of that test:
  simulated on the completed run's draws, the surrogate returns 1.0 at a tenth of the margin, where
  the test rejects in about one replicate in eight. The cap on draws with no recorded zone, also
  without effect on the branch, reads the worst cell, not the difference between conditions: the
  estimate describes only the draws that produced a zone. The case motivates three diagnostics:
  simulate the power of the test that decides, report support beside entropy, and compare dropped
  outputs between conditions. The claims concern these gates on one apparatus, two models and one
  prompt, not the channel's effect.
type: software
